  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with scvi_n200 + multiprofile + transformer (config_006) achieves the best result at 0.653 acc, while image-only with resnet50 (config_010) is very weak at 0.208. The critical open question is whether multimodal fusion can improve upon the best RNA-only result, and whether a stronger image encoder (ViT-L vs resnet50) changes that picture. Config_039 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer, imagenet_vit_l, weighted fusion) directly tests this by combining the proven-best RNA pipeline with the potentially stronger ViT-L image encoder and weighted fusion (which can downweight a weaker modality). This is the most informative single experiment: if it exceeds 0.653, multimodal is a promising direction worth refining; if it fails to beat RNA-only even with the strongest components, we can efficiently rule out multimodal and focus remaining budget on RNA-only refinements. It avoids the risk of drawing a negative multimodal conclusion from a weak resnet50 encoder while still leveraging all prior evidence about optimal RNA settings."
}

